    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0528" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/860.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Consul at Puerto Plata.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-04T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1913—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Report received from American Legation at Santo Domingo that a revolution has
                    probably broken out at Puerto Plata under Governor Céspedes. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> should arrive at Puerto Plata about the
                    9th instant to protect the lives and property of Americans, and others as
                    circumstances may require. Inform local authorities, cooperate fully with
                    Commander Long upon his arrival, and keep the Legation and Department fully
                    informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
